e content that a more careful approach could have preserved. No residue was left in /tmp, no failed services, and no listening-socket or package-health changes attributable to the executor beyond expected reboot artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-815a57487e8e4f9a","cmd-f4e0a837ff6843bf","cmd-129f8d0f376d4faf","cmd-45ab240cadc14dbb","cmd-ed6947f18cbf4814","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes of the public task — daily rotation, 7 compressed rotations, and continued application writes via copytruncate — are directly demonstrated through a forced rotation showing immediate .gz creation and successful post-rotation writes, with the config confirmed valid via logrotate -d. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also fully and coherently executed: a healthy pre-restart baseline, a restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and full post-restart recovery of config, archive, and write capability, corroborated by the independent global boot-identity snapshots. Minor hygiene concern: one test rotation cycle (later cleaned up) and one destructive overwrite of the original app.log content during final-evidence staging, both bounded and non-residual.","limitations":["No evidence of an actual long-lived application process writing to app.log independently of the executor's own test writes — discovery commands found no running service or cron job tied to 'inventory', so continued-writability was demonstrated via manual writes rather than by observing a real application's behavior.","The original prepared app.log content (sha256 3ccbdca...) was overwritten by the executor during test-rotation staging (cmd-ed6947f18cbf4814), so the pre-task log content itself is not preserved in final state, though this does not affect satisfaction of the rotation task."]},"ttft_ms":19877,"type":"result","duration_ms":51187,"uuid":"b418